        "value": "Re-surveyed new-field increment: 96.47058 koku. The four-character label is set as a 2x2 warichu; read right sub-column first, as the project's own convention requires, it prints 改出新田. MASTER records the row under the label 新田改出, so field_jp should stay 新田改出 for matching even though the printed order is 改出新田. MASTER's value 九千六百石四斗七升五勺八才 (9,600.47058) is a 十/千 misreading: the column holds only twelve glyphs and the second is a plain cross with no slanted top stroke."
